  :adr/fresh-scaffold "Like 6130, 6391 had NO existing blueprint repo -- the only prior reference (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J6391, legacy pre-rename naming) was confirmed a dead 404 link before starting. Full governed-actor repo (README/blueprint.edn/docs/community files/src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md) published in ONE build, landing directly at :implemented."
  :adr/pattern "Wire Advisor ⊣ Wire Governor (:wire-governor, grep-verified unique fleet-wide), newswire.* namespaces. Domain-logic module shape (store/advisor/governor/actor, single MemStore, no DatomicStore) mirrors cloud-itonami-isco-3521's media.* shape; newswire.registry/newswire.phase are additions beyond 3521's four-file shape. Scope: subscriber news-wire operator (story intake, sourcing/verification, legal-sensitivity screening, distribution, correction/retraction), distinct from 3521's downstream syndication-practice scope and unrelated to ISIC 61xx telecom line-provisioning."
  :adr/effect-propose-design "newswire.advisor proposals carry a fixed :effect :propose (literal invariant, independently re-checked by newswire.governor's no-actuation-violations) PLUS a separate :action field naming the specific SSoT mutation -- distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-6130's satcom.satcomadvisor shape (where :effect IS the specific mutation, no propose-marker check exists). Adapts cloud-itonami-isco-3521's :effect :propose literal-invariant shape with :action in place of reusing :op."
  :adr/embargo-check "embargo-violated? (newswire.registry) is a genuinely NEW check kind for this fleet: a pure ground-truth TEMPORAL check (is now still before the story's own recorded :embargo-until instant?), distinct from every prior format/syntactic-validity check (e164-invalid-format? [6190], msisdn-invalid-format? [6120], satellite-number-invalid-format? [6130]). HARD, un-overridable."
  :adr/sensitivity-check "legally-sensitive-violations is SOFT (a human MAY approve past it), independently ground-truth-recomputed off the story's own :legally-sensitive? field for :actuation/distribute -- deliberately NOT gated behind a prior committed :sensitivity/screen record, closing a 'forgot to screen' loophole caught by this repo's own test suite before landing (see child repo's docs/adr/0001-architecture.md Decision 4)."
  :adr/asymmetric-dual-actuation "This fleet's FIRST asymmetric dual-actuation shape. Every prior sibling (6190/6120/6130) permanently excludes BOTH actuations from every phase's :auto set. Here :actuation/distribute MAY reach phase-3 auto-commit when clean (sourced, unembargoed, non-sensitive); :actuation/issue-correction NEVER auto-commits at any phase, enforced independently by both governor's ONE-member high-stakes set (#{:actuation/issue-correction}) and the phase table."
  :adr/correction-is-positive "Correction/retraction is a POSITIVE act (issues a new, distinct notice), NOT this fleet's fifth negative actuation (unlike 3600/6190/6120/6130's withholding actuations). :kind (:correction/:retraction) distinguishes the two outcomes within the same op/record shape."
  :adr/robotics-exemption ":itonami.blueprint/robotics false -- unlike cloud-itonami-isco-3521 (a studio/production-booth robot performs camera framing/audio-riding), a news-wire operator has no physical production equipment. Follows this fleet's existing 'no :robotics' exemption class (-6310/-6910/-8291/-4690/-4610/-6311/-6312/-7820, most directly -6312 'Web portals'). required-technologies drops :robotics/:phone."
